[
  {"comment":"SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT. A flange on several connected edges with mitred corners (mitcad#1872, GitHub mitcad/Mitcad#337): t = 1, r = 1, K = 0.44, a 40 x 30 face, one Flange of tangent length 10 on its edges y = 0, x = 40 and y = 30 (two corners, the ends at x = 0 free). A bend's volume is 0.75 pi and its flat area 0.72 pi per mm of its width. Bisect, Inside, gap g: each flange keeps g/2 off the vertical 45-degree plane through the corner and the walls' inner corner; a wall ends on the plane at its inner surface (x <= 39 - g/sqrt2 for y = 0), a bend where its tangent line on the face meets it (x <= 38 - g/sqrt2); the face is cut back 2 mm (the setback) along the three edges, 38 x 26 left. Walls 10 (39 - g/sqrt2) + 10 (28 - sqrt2 g) + 10 (39 - g/sqrt2), bends 102 - 2 sqrt2 g mm wide."},
